<title>USA: Chase unit sells $300 mln capital securities.</title>
<headline>Chase unit sells $300 mln capital securities.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue of floating rate capital securities from Chase Capital III, a unit of Chase Manhattan Corp, was priced on Tuesday, according to lead manager Chase Securities Inc.</p>
<p>BORROWER CHASE CAPITAL III</p>
<p>AMT $300 MLN	 COUPON 3MO LIBOR +55 MATURITY 3/01/2027</p>
<p>TYPE FLT-RATE CAP  ISS PRICE 98.558     FIRST PAY DATE 9/1/97</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S AA3   YIELD LIBOR +67.5    PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P BBB-PLUS			     CALLABLE NON CALL 10</p>
<p>((U.S. corporate bond unit, 212 859-1672))</p>
